{"name":"Wild Axolotl","hex":"#63775a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wild","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Untamed; not domesticated.","Especially, being of the wild type: being of an unbroken ancestral line of undomesticated animals, as opposed to being feral, being an undomesticated animal whose ancestors were domesticated."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Inaccurately; not on target.","Intended to be synchronized with film or video but recorded separately."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wild"},{"term":"axolotl","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A critically endangered salamander found in the elevated lakes of Mexico, Ambystoma mexicanum."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/axolotl"}],"entries":[{"title":"Axolotl","blocks":[{"text":"The axolotl is a species of mole salamander. It is neotenic, reaching sexual maturity without undergoing metamorphosis, and the adults remain fully aquatic with obvious external gills. Axolotls may be difficult to distinguish from the larval stage of other neotenic adult mole salamanders, in particular the tiger salamander, or other species such as mudpuppies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Axolotl_ganz.jpg/330px-Axolotl_ganz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axolotl"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Axolot%27s_head_%28Ambystoma_mexicanum%29.jpg/500px-Axolot%27s_head_%28Ambystoma_mexicanum%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Axolot%27s_head_%28Ambystoma_mexicanum%29.jpg/1280px-Axolot%27s_head_%28Ambystoma_mexicanum%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Axolot%27s_head_%28Ambysto